using API gateway we can access APIS from one single port like - http://localhost:5000/products  using 5000


// redis implemention

API Gateway
Rate Limiting
1. Use Redis for Rate Limiting
(for every request, the Gateway checks Redis — 'Has this user crossed the limit?' If yes, it blocks the request. Otherwise, it lets it through)
2. Start Redis via docker - docker run -d -p 6379:6379 redis
3. Add Required Dependencies


why we are using redis -


The flow is:
1. First request: Redis doesn't have the product, so Spring Boot fetches it from the database and saves a copy in Redis.
2. Second request: Redis already has the product, so Spring Boot returns it without querying the database.
3. More requests: Spring Boot can keep returning the cached copy until it expires or gets updated.

For example, Redis might store:
Key: rate_limit:user101
Value: 5
Expiry: 60 seconds


Each request increments the counter. Redis is fast at this because it stores data in memory.

git bash command - for i in {1..10}; do curl -X GET "http://localhost:6001/orders/ord-50b0423a"; done

used git bash command to send multiple request at a time because postman se nahi hoga -

First 5 requests → Allowed ✅

6th request → Rejected with HTTP 429 Too Many Requests ❌

After the limit resets → Requests are allowed again.


